+    into b.kscratch.out[lo:lo + n], its parity flipped, its conv window shifted; a piece marked inside its rows (OTS
+    0121) runs as kda_rows' two calls, the state and conv window between them kept, its second call in a second
+    launch with the other marked pieces' (the first takes the conv window the first part shifted). Pieces are
+    independent (each reads and writes only its own stream's state and conv window), so running their chains
+    together, then their commits, changes no bit. Without the chunked kernel, under TF_GLM_KDA_PIECES=0, or for one
